PATCH 115: rebase the version-string text renderer to the far string segment (a358 width + 5591 glyph loop).

e9f0 (and e459/e4bb) draw the "AF-FD ..." version string:
    mov ax,6 ; mov es,[DGROUP:0x70] ; mov si,<str-off> ; lcall 0xf69:0xacc8 (=FUN_1000_a358 width)
    ... shr ax,1 ; bx=0xa0-ax/2 ; ax=0xbf ; cl=<color> ; lcall 0xf69:0xace0 (=FUN_1000_a370 draw)
The string bytes live in the far string data segment (es=[DGROUP:0x70]=0x2d74); Ghidra dropped that ES
base at every string read, leaving the raw offset (e.g. 0x44fe) dereferenced as a host pointer -> SEGV.
- FUN_1000_a358 (asm 0x1a358): text-width = char-count(<=0xa0) * width; rebase si to [0x70]:off.
- FUN_1000_5591 + its 0x1558b thunk (asm 0x15591): the glyph loop `lods es:[si]->al; c684(al)` with
  es HARDCODED to 0x2d74 in the asm.  Rebuild the es base and pass the char in al to the per-glyph
  blitter DGROUP:0x684 (both dropped by Ghidra: string read as host ptr, c684 called with no char).
Asm-verified 0x1a358, 0x15591/0x1558b.  (The deeper glyph-blit subtree c684->1e88 is a further frontier.)
